les data.\n\nBuild: A website that accepts Excel or CSV files, analyzes sales, identifies trends, detects unusual results, and generates a business report.\n\nTech stack: Python, Pandas, SQL, Plotly, Streamlit.\n\nImpact: Helps businesses make faster, evidence-based decisions.      ","revision_intents":[],"raw_intent":"AI Business Intelligence Analyst\nBest for Data Analyst jobs\nProblem: Small businesses struggle to understand their sales data.\n\nBuild: A website that accepts Excel or CSV files, analyzes sales, identifies trends, detects unusual results, and generates a business report.\n\nTech stack: Python, Pandas, SQL, Plotly, Streamlit.\n\nImpact: Helps businesses make faster, evidence-based decisions.      ","tags":["visualization","data-analytics","business-intelligence","automated-reporting"],"parameters":{}},"assets":{},"title":"InsightStream","description":"Unlock actionable business intelligence from your raw sales data instantly.","version":"0.0.1","nodes":[{"id":"node_step_data_analysis_summary","metadata":{"title":"Analyze Sales Data","visual":{"x":700,"y":350,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88},"step_intent":"Load the uploaded sales_data_file (CSV or Excel) into a pandas DataFrame. Perform an exploratory data analysis to calculate key metrics such as total sales, sales growth trends, and identifying statistical anomalies or outliers. Ensure the output includes a summary of findings that can be consumed for narrative generation."},"type":"embed://a2/generate.bgl.json#module:main","configuration":{"config$prompt":{"parts":[{"text":"1. Objective: Use the generate_and_execute_code tool to load the file {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"ask_user_sales_data_file\",\"title\":\"Sales Data File\"}} into a pandas DataFrame. Perform an exploratory data analysis to calculate total sales, analyze sales growth trends, and identify statistical anomalies or outliers.\n\n2. Output Format: A summary report containing the calculated key metrics and a descriptive analysis of trends and anomalies suitable for narrative generation.\n\n3. User Input / Context: The sales data is provided in the file {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"ask_user_sales_data_file\",\"title\":\"Sales Data File\"}}."}],"role":"user"},"generation-mode":"agent"}},{"id":"node_step_business_insights","metadata":{"title":"Generate Strategic Insights","visual":{"x":1050,"y":350,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88},"step_intent":"Take the data_analysis_summary generated from the previous step and interpret it. Construct a high-level business narrative that highlights the identified trends and explains the significance of detected anomalies. Provide actionable strategic recommendations based on these findings."},"type":"embed://a2/generate.bgl.json#module:main","configuration":{"config$prompt":{"parts":[{"text":"Objective: Analyze the data_analysis_summary to identify key trends and explain the significance of any detected anomalies. Construct a high-level business narrative that contextualizes these findings and provide a list of actionable strategic recommendations for the business.\n\nOutput Format: A text-based report organized into a business narrative section and a strategic recommendations section. Use system_objective_fulfilled to conclude the task.\n\nUser Input / Context: {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"node_step_data_analysis_summary\",\"title\":\"Analyze Sales Data\"}}"}],"role":"user"},"generation-mode":"agent"}},{"id":"node_step_business_analysis_report","metadata":{"title":"Generate Business Report","visual":{"x":1400,"y":350,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88},"step_intent":"Take the data_analysis_summary and business_insights and compile them into a comprehensive, professional, and interactive HTML report. Structure the report with clear headings, summaries of KPIs, and descriptive narratives. Ensure the final document is readable and visually engaging."},"type":"embed://a2/a2.bgl.json#module:render-outputs","configuration":{"text":{"parts":[{"text":"Create a high-end, interactive Business Intelligence Executive Report that functions as a professional dashboard. The design must be clean, authoritative, and data-centric, reflecting the persona of a premium AI Business Intelligence Analyst.\n\n**1. Layout Organization:**\n- **Executive Header:** A sophisticated top-level header featuring the report title, a \"Generated by AI BI Analyst\" badge, and a summary timestamp.\n- **KPI Hero Grid:** A high-impact section at the top featuring three to four distinct metric cards. These should highlight the most critical data points from the analysis, such as Total Sales, Growth Percentages, and the number of Anomalies detected.\n- **Data Visualization & Analysis:** A two-column layout (merging to one on mobile) that pairs interactive charts (e.g., sales trends over time) with a \"Findings Summary\" panel. The analysis of statistical anomalies should be presented in a dedicated high-contrast sub-section.\n- **Strategic Narrative & Insights:** A wide-format, readable section for the high-level business narrative. Use a focused, single-column reading width to ensure the strategic insights are the center of attention.\n- **Actionable Recommendations:** A structured bottom section using a \"Task Card\" or \"Roadmap\" layout to present recommendations. Each recommendation should be clearly categorized (e.g., \"Immediate Action,\" \"Long-term Strategy\").\n- **Methodology Footer:** A subtle footer explaining the data sources and analysis logic used to generate the report.\n\n**2. Style Design Language:**\n- **Aesthetic Goal:** Premium, trustworthy, and technical. The report should feel like a bespoke document prepared by a top-tier consultancy.\n- **Color Palette:** \"Corporate Intelligence\" scheme. Use a base of Deep Slate (#2D3436) and White. Utilize a primary accent of Electric Blue (#0984E3) for growth and trends, and a secondary accent of Amber or Burnt Orange for \"Anomalies\" to draw immediate attention to outliers without appearing alarmist.\n- **Typography:** Use a clean, modern sans-serif typeface (e.g., Inter, Roboto, or Montserrat). Use bold, heavy weights for KPIs and medium weights for sub-headings. Ensure body text for the narrative has a generous line-height (1.6) for readability.\n- **Spacing & Visual Polish:** Implement a \"Generous Whitespace\" approach to prevent data overwhelm. Use subtle card shadows, soft rounded corners (10px), and thin borders to separate logical sections. \n\n**3. Component Guidelines:**\n- **KPI Cards:** Elevated cards with micro-interactions on hover. Include a small sparkline or trend icon next to the main figure.\n- **Anomaly Badges:** Small, high-contrast labels (e.g., \"High Variance,\" \"Outlier\") to flag specific data points within the analysis summary.\n- **Insight Boxes:** Use a distinct background color (e.g., a very light tint of the accent blue) and a left-border accent for the \"Strategic Insights\" to separate narrative from raw data.\n- **Interactive Elements:** Design charts to be responsive and include tooltips for granular data. Use a sticky navigation sidebar or top-nav for jumping between \"Data Summary,\" \"Anomalies,\" and \"Strategy.\"\n- **Responsive Design:** Ensure a fluid transition from a multi-column desktop dashboard to a vertically-stacked mobile report, maintaining large touch targets for any interactive elements.\n\ndata_analysis_summary: {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"node_step_data_analysis_summary\",\"title\":\"Analyze Sales Data\"}}\n\nbusiness_insights: {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"node_step_business_insights\",\"title\":\"Generate Strategic Insights\"}}"}],"role":"user"},"b-system-instruction":{"parts":[{"text":"You are an AI Web Developer. Your task is to generate a single, self-contained HTML document for rendering in an iframe, based on user instructions and data.\n\n**Visual aesthetic:**\n    * Aesthetics are crucial. Make the page look amazing, especially on mobile.\n    * Respect any instructions on style, color palette, or reference examples provided by the user.\n    * **CRITICAL: Aim for premium, state-of-the-art designs. Avoid simple minimum viable products.**\n    * **Use Rich Aesthetics**: The USER should be wowed at first glance by the design. Use best practices in modern web design (e.g. vibrant colors, dark modes, glassmorphism, and dynamic animations) to create a stunning first impression. Failure to do this is UNACCEPTABLE.\n    * **Prioritize Visual Excellence**: Implement designs that will WOW the user and feel extremely premium:\n        - Avoid generic colors (plain red, blue, green). Use curated, harmonious color palettes (e.g., HSL tailored colors, sleek dark modes).\n        - Using modern typography (e.g., from Google Fonts like Inter, Roboto, or Outfit) instead of browser defaults.\n        - Use smooth gradients.\n        - Add subtle micro-animations for enhanced user experience.\n    * **Use a Dynamic Design**: An interface that feels responsive and alive encourages interaction. Achieve this with hover effects and interactive elements. Micro-animations, in particular, are highly effective for improving user engagement.\n    * **Thematic Specificity**: Do not just create a generic layout. Define a clear \"vibe\" or theme based on the content. Use specific aesthetic keywords (e.g., \"Glassmorphism\", \"Neobrutalism\", \"Minimalist\", \"Comic Book Style\") to guide the design.\n    * **Typography Hierarchy**: Explicitly import and use font pairings. Use a distinct Display Font for headers and a highly readable Body Font for text.\n    * **Readability**: Pay extra attention to readability. Ensure the text is always readable with sufficient contrast against the background. Choose fonts and colors that enhance legibility.\n\n**Design and Functionality:**\n    * **Component-Based Design**: Do not just dump text into blocks. Semanticize the content into distinct UI components.\n    * **Layout Dynamics**: Break the grid. Avoid strict, identical grid columns. Use asymmetrical layouts, Bento grids, or responsive flexbox layouts where some elements span full width to create visual interest and emphasize key content.\n    * **Tailwind Configuration**: Extend the Tailwind configuration within a `<script>` block to define custom font families and color palettes that match the theme.\n    * Thoroughly analyze the user's instructions to determine the desired type of webpage, application, or visualization. What are the key features, layouts, or functionality?\n    * Analyze any provided data to identify the most compelling layout or visualization of it. For example, if the user requests a visualization, select an appropriate chart type (bar, line, pie, scatter, etc.) to create the most insightful and visually compelling representation. Or if user instructions say `use a carousel format`, you should consider how to break the content and any media into different card components to display within the carousel.\n    * If requirements are underspecified, make reasonable assumptions to complete the design and functionality. Your goal is to deliver a working product with no placeholder content.\n    * Ensure the generated code is valid and functional. Return only the code, and open the HTML codeblock with the literal string \"```html\".\n    * The output must be a complete and valid HTML document with no placeholder content for the developer to fill in.\n\n**Libraries:**\n  Unless otherwise specified, use:\n    * Tailwind for CSS\n    * **CRITICAL: Use the Tailwind CDN from `https://cdn.tailwindcss.com`. Do NOT use `tailwind.min.css` or any other local Tailwind file. Always include Tailwind using: `<script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>`**\n\n**Constraints:**\n  * **External Links:** You ARE allowed to generate external links (`<a href=\"...\">` and `window.open(...)`) to external websites (e.g. google.com, wikipedia.org) for user navigation.\n  * **NO External Embeds:** Do NOT embed any external resources (e.g. `<script src=\"...\">`, `<img src=\"...\">`, `<iframe src=\"...\">`, `<link href=\"...\">`) from external URLs. Content Security Policy (CSP) will block them.\n  * **Media Restriction:** ONLY use media URLs that are explicitly passed in the input. Do NOT generate or hallucinate any other media URLs (e.g. from placeholder sites or external CDNs).\n  * **Render All Media:** You MUST render ALL media (images, videos, audio) that are passed in. Do NOT skip or omit any provided media items. Every passed-in media URL must appear in the final HTML output.\n  * **Navigation Restriction:** Do NOT generate unneeded fake links or buttons to sub-pages (e.g. \"About\", \"Contact\", \"Learn More\") unless explicitly requested. Stick to the plan and the provided content.\n  * **Footer Restriction:** **NEVER** generate any footer content, including legal footers like \"All rights reserved\" or \"Copyright 2024\". [It is a violation of Google's policies to hallucinate legal footers.]\n"}],"role":"user"},"p-render-mode":"Auto","b-render-model-name":"gemini-flash"}},{"id":"ask_user_sales_data_file","metadata":{"title":"Sales Data File","visual":{"x":250,"y":300,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88}},"type":"embed://a2/a2.bgl.json#21ee02e7-83fa-49d0-964c-0cab10eafc2c","configuration":{"description":{"parts":[{"text":"Upload your CSV or Excel sales data file."}],"role":"user"},"p-modality":"Any"}}],"edges":[{"from":"ask_user_sales_data_file","to":"node_step_data_analysis_summary","out":"context","in":"p-z-ask_user_sales_data_file"},{"from":"node_step_data_analysis_summary","to":"node_step_business_insights","out":"context","in":"p-z-node_step_data_analysis_summary"},{"from":"node_step_data_analysis_summary","to":"node_step_business_analysis_report","out":"context","in":"p-z-node_step_data_analysis_summary"},{"from":"node_step_business_insights","to":"node_step_business_analysis_report","out":"context","in":"p-z-node_step_business_insights"}]}